1. d4 Nf6 2. Bf4 c5 {Plan map. 1: challenge the center immediately. 2: after e3, exchange on d4 and use ...Qb6 to ask how White defends b2 and d4. 3: against Nc3, prefer ...a6 before ...d5 so Nb5 is not annoying. 4: after Nf3, pin with ...Bg4. 5: develop ...e6 and ...Bd6, then move the queen from b6 to c7 once b6 has done its job. 6: expand with ...b5, use the c-file, and reroute a knight to c4. 7: if White damages their kingside, cover with ...g6, use ...Nh5, and swing the queen to h4. 8: when attacking, open a second front with ...e5 or switch back to c2/d5 targets.} 3. e3 cxd4 4. exd4 Qb6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Rb1 d5 7. Nf3 Bg4 8. Be2 Nc6 9. Be3 e6 10. O-O Bd6 11. h3 Bh5 12. a3 Qc7 13. Qd2 O-O 14. Kh1 b5 15. b4 Rfc8 16. Bd3 Bxf3 17. gxf3 Nb8 18. Rg1 g6 19. Ne2 Nh5 20. f4 Qd8 21. Rg4 Nxf4 22. Bxf4 Qh4 *
